<title>CHINA: KOOKMIN SEEN PLANNING US$100 MLN FRN.</title>
<headline>KOOKMIN SEEN PLANNING US$100 MLN FRN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kookmin Bank is seen planning a US$100 million floating rate note issue, bankers said.</p>
<p>They said the facility has a final maturity of three years with annual put and call options.</p>
<p>The notes are expected to pay a margin &quot;in the mid 40's&quot; basis points over the London Interbank Offered Rate, bankers said.</p>
<p>Sources said BOT-Mitsuibishi and ABN Amro have submitted bidding proposals. However, no mandate has been formally awarded yet.</p>
<p>The facility is expected to be issued off the borrower's US$1.5 billion Medium Term Note Programme.</p>
<p>--Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
</text>
